{
  "cases": [
    {
      "i": 14715,
      "title": "Analytics Dashboard returns HTTP 429 and malformed JSON in Dev Environment",
      "description": "We are experiencing critical issues with the Analytics Dashboard in our development environment (ME region). When attempting to load reports, the application frequently hangs before returning an HTTP 429 error. In several instances, if the request doesn't fail with 429, the response payload is malformed JSON, causing the frontend to crash. Additionally, we suspect an upstream dependency timeout is contributing to these failures, as the dashboard waits indefinitely before throwing the error. This is blocking approximately 3,123 developers from accessing analytics data."
    },
    {
      "i": 14716,
      "title": "Payment Gateway v2 API schema errors in US-East Staging",
      "description": "Our staging environment in US-East is failing to process transactions via Payment Gateway v2. We are receiving API schema validation errors when submitting payment requests. It is unclear if the issue lies with the Payment Gateway interface itself or if the payload being sent to the Currency Conversion Service is incompatible with the expected schema. This is critical as it prevents us from validating new payment flows for 1,743 test users."
    },
    {
      "i": 14717,
      "title": "Mobile app slowness related to Currency Converter and Adjustments",
      "description": "Users in the LATAM production environment are reporting significant slowness in the mobile application. The delays seem to occur when financial transactions are being calculated or displayed. We are seeing slow response times generally, but it is difficult to isolate whether the bottleneck is in the Currency Converter or the Credit/Debit Adjustment Service, as both components appear to be involved in the affected user journeys. No specific business impact has been flagged yet, but user experience is degraded."
    },
    {
      "i": 14718,
      "title": "Self-Service Hub UI element not rendering in US-East Staging",
      "description": "In the US-East staging environment, a specific UI element on the Self-Service Hub is failing to render. The element is completely invisible to the user, preventing them from interacting with that section of the dashboard. This issue affects 74 internal testers and is currently blocking the validation of new self-service features. The rest of the interface loads normally."
    },
    {
      "i": 14719,
      "title": "Currency Converter issues causing subscription renewal and invoice errors",
      "description": "We are seeing problems with the Currency Converter in the LATAM production environment. Several users (approx. 9) are reporting that their subscriptions have not renewed despite payment being attempted. Furthermore, when invoices are generated, the amounts appear incorrect. We believe the Currency Converter is misapplying exchange rates or failing to communicate renewal status correctly, leading to these billing discrepancies."
    },
    {
      "i": 14720,
      "title": "Audit log gaps and incomplete compliance reports in Analytics Dashboard (LATAM Prod)",
      "description": "During our regular review of the Analytics Dashboard in the LATAM production environment, we detected gaps in the audit logs for two specific administrative accounts. Consequently, the compliance reports generated for these users are incomplete. The dashboard is not capturing certain actions, resulting in missing data points in the final export. This is a low-impact issue currently affecting only 2 users but needs to be resolved for audit integrity."
    },
    {
      "i": 14721,
      "title": "Undercharging on Payment Gateway v2 (ANZ Prod)",
      "description": "We have identified an issue in the ANZ production environment where Payment Gateway v2 is undercharging customers. Approximately 43 accounts have been affected. We are confident this is caused by database contention on our end, as we noticed high lock waits during the transaction processing windows. The gateway is failing to apply the correct amount due to this resource conflict, resulting in lower-than-expected charges."
    },
    {
      "i": 14722,
      "title": "Refunds not reflecting in LATAM Production",
      "description": "Refund transactions initiated through Payment Gateway v2 in the LATAM production environment are not being reflected in customer accounts. About 87 users are affected. We believe this is definitely an incorrect load balancer routing issue. It seems that refund requests are being sent to a stale or incorrect backend instance that is not updating the ledger properly, causing the refunds to disappear or remain pending indefinitely."
    },
    {
      "i": 14723,
      "title": "Account lockouts in APAC SSO Integration Module",
      "description": "Six users in the APAC region are experiencing account lockouts when trying to access systems via the SSO Integration Module. We suspect this is happening because of insufficient monitoring and alerting on our side. The system likely triggered a security lockout without notifying us or the users, and we missed the early warning signs. We need to adjust the SSO configuration to prevent these silent lockouts from occurring."
    },
    {
      "i": 14724,
      "title": "MFA prompts missing, SSO loops, and duplicate accounts in LATAM Prod",
      "description": "We are encountering a mix of authentication issues in the LATAM production environment involving Payment Gateway v2. Users are not receiving MFA prompts when expected, some are stuck in SSO redirect loops, and in a few cases, duplicate accounts are being created. It is unclear if this is a defect in the Payment Gateway's authentication flow or an issue with the Usage Metering Service misidentifying the user sessions. This is impacting 284 users with high severity."
    },
    {
      "i": 14725,
      "title": "Feedback Collector webhooks and JSON issues",
      "description": "The Feedback Collector isn't working right. Webhooks aren't firing and when we do get data it's JSON that doesn't parse. A few people are complaining. Not sure exactly when it started or which specific error codes we are getting but it's happening on US-East prod. Please check."
    },
    {
      "i": 14726,
      "title": "Overcharging detected on Payment Gateway v2 (EU-Central Prod)",
      "description": "We have observed instances of overcharging in the EU-Central production environment. Approximately 21 customers have been billed more than the expected amount for their subscriptions. The issue appears isolated to specific transaction types processed through Payment Gateway v2. We have verified that the correct prices are configured in our system, so the error seems to originate from the gateway calculation logic. This requires immediate attention to refund affected users."
    },
    {
      "i": 14727,
      "title": "HTTP 403 and elevated privileges observed in Session Controller (ME Prod)",
      "description": "In the Middle East production environment, users of the Session Controller are receiving HTTP 403 Forbidden errors. Additionally, we have observed that some users are displaying elevated privileges that they should not have, or the system is incorrectly granting them access before failing with a 403. This inconsistency is affecting 87 users and poses a potential security concern regarding privilege management. We need to investigate why valid sessions are being rejected while unauthorized access attempts are partially succeeding."
    },
    {
      "i": 14728,
      "title": "Audit log missing entries and incomplete compliance reports (EU-West Prod)",
      "description": "We are noticing missing entries in the audit logs for transactions processed via Payment Gateway v2 in the EU-West production environment. This has resulted in incomplete compliance reports for 21 users. The dashboard shows the transactions were successful, but the detailed audit trail is absent. We believe the Payment Gateway is failing to write the correct logs to its internal store. No third-party integrations have changed recently that we are aware of."
    },
    {
      "i": 14729,
      "title": "Undercharge and incorrect invoice in Billing Engine (US-West Dev)",
      "description": "In our US-West development environment, the Billing Engine is generating invoices with incorrect amounts. Specifically, we are seeing undercharges on a test account (1 user affected). The line items do not match the expected configuration for this development scenario. We have verified the input data is correct, so the issue lies within the Billing Engine's calculation or template rendering logic."
    }
  ]
